A contour line of a function of two variables is a curve along which the function has a constant value, so that the curve joins points of equal value of the state. 
It is a plane section of the three-dimensional graph of a function f(x, y) parallel to the (x, y)-plane. 
More generally, a contour line for a function of two varibales is a curve connecting points where the function has the same particular value. 


